cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "funcprox: a neural network as a device for function approximation"
abstract: >-
  Neural networks built from scratch in NumPy (MLP, SIREN, Fourier features, Kolmogorov-Arnold
  networks, trained with Adam or Levenberg-Marquardt) approximate one-, two- and three-input
  functions, typed, measured or drawn by hand, next to classical fits. Every model is scored
  against the exact function, including a missing middle it never saw. Includes a sensitivity
  study of the network's settings and a browser interface.
type: software
authors:
